{number: 38}
{title: When the Roll is Called Up}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] When the trumpet of the Lord shall sound, and time shall be no more,
And the morning breaks, eternal, bright and [Eb7] fair;
When the [Ab] saved of earth shall gather over on the other shore,
And the [Ab] roll is called up [Eb7] yonder, I'll be [Ab] there.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
When the [Ab] roll is called up yonder,
When the [Eb7] roll is called up yonder,
When the [Ab] roll is called up [Db] yonder,
When the [Ab] roll is called up [Eb7] yonder, I'll be [Ab] there.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
On [Ab] that bright and cloudless morning when the dead in Christ shall rise,
And the glory of His resurrection [Eb7] share;
When His [Ab] chosen ones shall gather to their home beyond the skies,
And the [Ab] roll is called up [Eb7] yonder, I'll be [Ab] there.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Let [Ab] us labor for the Master from the dawn till setting sun,
Let us talk of all His wondrous love and [Eb7] care;
Then when [Ab] all of life is over, and our work on earth is done,
And the [Ab] roll is called up [Eb7] yonder, I'll be [Ab] there.
{end_of_verse}
